From: Switch-CrOS Authors
Subject: [PATCH] shill: don't DCHECK on missing MAC for Linux < 4.14 interfaces

DeviceInfo::DelayedDeviceCreationTask DCHECKs that any non-Tunnel,
non-Unknown interface whose arp_type != ARPHRD_RAWIP has a MAC address.
ARPHRD_RAWIP was only introduced in Linux 4.14 — on older kernels (the
Switch port runs L4T 4.9), cellular and certain virtual interfaces
legitimately have no MAC address and a non-ARPHRD_RAWIP arp_type, so
this DCHECK fires and shill aborts every ~5 seconds (it respawns on
every uevent for the device).

The DCHECK isn't a real invariant — CreateDevice() below it handles an
empty mac_address. Soft-fail by skipping device creation with a
warning instead of aborting.

Affects only Linux < 4.14 systems; on modern kernels this branch never
executes because arp_type == ARPHRD_RAWIP for any interface that would
have triggered it.

--- a/device_info.cc
+++ b/device_info.cc
@@ -1275,10 +1275,18 @@
         infos_[dev_index].mac_address;
     int arp_type = GetDeviceArpType(link_name);
 
-    // NB: ARHRD_RAWIP was introduced in kernel 4.14.
+    // NB: ARPHRD_RAWIP was introduced in kernel 4.14.  On older kernels
+    // (e.g., Switch L4T 4.9), cellular/virtual interfaces may legitimately
+    // have neither a MAC address nor ARPHRD_RAWIP, so DCHECKing here
+    // would abort the process on every uevent.  Skip the device instead.
     if (technology != Technology::kTunnel &&
         technology != Technology::kUnknown && arp_type != ARPHRD_RAWIP) {
-      DCHECK(mac_address.has_value());
+      if (!mac_address.has_value()) {
+        LOG(WARNING) << __func__ << ": skipping " << link_name
+                     << " (technology=" << technology
+                     << ", arp_type=" << arp_type << "): no MAC address";
+        continue;
+      }
     }
 
     DeviceRefPtr device =
